At one point troll dancing was common because regenerated
troll got the same chances of initial inventory as generated
trolls.  You could get vast piles of polypile fodder doing it.  As
a result the DevTeam changed regenerated trolls to have much
lower odds of giving items and the details or regeneration were
probably tuned to ensure any one troll would eventually rot
away before regenerating.

Versions that allowed unlimited wishes and so on were also
changed to disallow that.

So historically the DevTeam has closed loopholes in the game
that give unlimited items.  Pudding farming is the best
known example at the moment.

I repeat another sentiment - I view pudding farming as an
abuse not a cheat.  I do in fact use the split function of
puddings to make sure I have as many resistance intrinsics
as I'll be able to get from them.  I will make a few dozen as
sacrifice fodder if I encounter a pudding on an altar level.
I may some day dig out a level with an altar to have enough
puddings to altar dance my way to AC=-40 or better but so
far I've stopped when I got all the intrinsic resistances.

There's also quest levels not respecting extinction numbers.
Here's why I don't view that as an abuse - The rate of monster
generation continues without change on those levels.  If you
play an extinctionist and try to get your score to MAXINT on
a quest level gradually all other monster types reach their
extinction quota and you're down to the list of special quest
monster types.  You can eventually starve doing that, but
if you don't the game just never stops.  If it takes forever I
don't see it as an abuse.

> > In my opinion, pudding farming, nurse dancing,
> > foocubus dancing, n1000s'ing, rubber chicken wielding all have
> > inherent risks to balance their gains.

They all also have built-in expirations.  Each nurse will
eventually disappear out of the game and there are a
limited number of them.    Foocubi eventually cancel and
there are a limited number of them.  Rubber chickens
eventually rot away and there are a limited number of
them that might be generated.  Even using a wish on a
rubber chicken is a limited activity.

